<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Workflow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <Workflow> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW FILE, 2026-08-28. Underwriting__c had no workflow metadata before this change.

        🔴 UPDATED 2026-09-02, item 1 + item 2 of agent-output/three-gaps-design-2026-09-02.md,
        ONE COMBINED EDIT. Two field updates ADDED (Set_UW_Approval_Pending, Clear_UW_Approval_
        Pending — the pending UI flag, same mechanism as Disposition__c.Approval_Pending__c) and
        UW_Status_Approved REMOVED (item 2, option (a): Underwriting__c.Status__c is being retired
        as a strict-subset duplicate of Stage__c; see objects/Underwriting__c/fields/Status__c
        .field-meta.xml's own header before it is deleted. The field removal itself, and this
        field update's deletion, land in a LATER wave once the Apex classes that reference
        Status__c compile clean without it — do not delete Status__c before that Apex lands).

        🔴 FOUR FIELD UPDATES, NO WORKFLOW RULE. All four are fired ONLY by
        approvalProcesses/Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval, as initialSubmissionActions /
        finalApprovalActions / finalRejectionActions / recallActions. Do not add a <rules>
        element: an active rule writing any of these fields on an ordinary edit would fake an
        approval or strand the pending flag.

        🔴 STAGE/STATUS REJECTION HANDLING IS STILL DROPPED, BY DESIGN (user decision D2,
        UNCHANGED). Stage__c never changes on rejection - the entry criterion is Stage__c =
        'In Progress' and nothing moves it during the pending window - so a rejection field
        update keyed on Stage__c would be a same-value no-op even if one were added. On rejection
        the record simply stays at Stage__c = 'In Progress' and only the approval history shows
        the decision. Opportunity.Underwriting_Complete__c is NOT cleared on reject any more
        (accepted, documented regression from the now-inert Opportunity.UW_Reopen_For_Revision) -
        see the approval process file's own header for the full rationale.
        ⚠ WHAT CHANGED: the approval process NOW carries a finalRejectionActions block for the
        FIRST time — but it fires ONLY Clear_UW_Approval_Pending below, not a Stage__c/Status__c
        write. D2's substance (no stage rewind on reject) is unchanged; only the pending UI flag
        gets a clear-on-reject path, because without one a rejected record would stay flagged
        pending forever with the Submit button permanently hidden - worse than the defect being
        fixed.

        THE CHILD-OBJECT HALF of moving the approval onto Underwriting__c. All four field updates
        write only this record's own fields - required, because Underwriting__c.Opportunity__c
        is a Lookup, not a Master-Detail, so an approval process on this object cannot
        field-update the parent Opportunity at all. The parent mirror
        (UW_Approved__c / Underwriting_Status__c / UW_Approved_By__c / UW_Approval_Date__c) is
        written separately by flows/Underwriting_Approval_Sync.flow-meta.xml, entry-scoped on
        Stage__c transitioning to 'Approved', calling UnderwritingApprovalStampService - UNCHANGED
        by this edit; that flow reads Stage__c, never Status__c (confirmed by repo grep, C6 in the
        three-gaps design), so removing UW_Status_Approved does not touch it.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. This file must land BEFORE
        approvalProcesses/Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval.approvalProcess-meta.xml, which
        references all four field updates by name. And objects/Underwriting__c/fields
        /Approval_Pending__c.field-meta.xml must land BEFORE this file.
    -->
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Clear_UW_Approval_Pending</fullName>
        <description>Clears the approval pending UI flag. Fired by Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval on final approval (2nd action with UW_Stage_Approved), final rejection and recall. Clearing on all three stops Submit for Approval staying hidden.</description>
        <field>Approval_Pending__c</field>
        <literalValue>0</literalValue>
        <name>Clear UW Approval Pending</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Set_UW_Approval_Pending</fullName>
        <description>Sets the approval pending UI flag. Fired as an initialSubmissionActions entry by Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval. The third criterion on Underwriting_Record_Page's Submit for Approval Dynamic Action hides the button while it is true.</description>
        <field>Approval_Pending__c</field>
        <literalValue>1</literalValue>
        <name>Set UW Approval Pending</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>UW_Stage_Approved</fullName>
        <description>Final approval action of Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval. Sets Stage to Approved on this Underwriting record.</description>
        <field>Stage__c</field>
        <literalValue>Approved</literalValue>
        <name>UW Stage Approved</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
</Workflow>
